{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:df09b78b118831b2","name":"FX-6 Medical Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-df09b78b118831b2","title":"FX-6 Medical Droid","revision":19450,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:59:58Z","sha256":"c8619875bf701793c0baf7b47c7b5855b4926125b8714d3520f1ee91e0f9e2ba","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19450","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=FX-6%20Medical%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-df09b78b118831b2","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The FX-6 Medical Droid was built during ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"}," as a mobile, autonomous, skill medical assistant to field medics fighting on the front line. The Grand Army of the Republic even dropped the FX-6 Droids into areas where fighting was planned (or already going on) to grant additional medical aid to clone forces. Of course, this also means that numerous battlefields were littered with FX-6s in various stats of repair, and more than one scavenger took the opportunity to add a few to their inventory.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The FX-6 is able to move over many different terrains with its three casters, a trick not available to many FX models. Many FX Droids are immobile, but the FX-6 has a strong sense of balance and good movement ability over any reasonably even terrain. This additional capacity comes at the price of not including a personality package or even a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vocabulator"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vocabulator","referenceId":"reference:a28880d579fbd223"},", leaving the Droid able to communicate only through readout panels. Although this limitation gives it a sinister bedside manner, it has no impact on the Droid's ability and desire to render medical assistance. Equipped with a ring of sensors, numerous surgical tools, and multiple appendages, an FX-6 can be equipped to deal with most medical problems and to treat any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Produced in vast numbers and seeded on dozens of battlefields, the FX-6 is a common sight in the years after ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},". Designed as an assistant, the model is capable of performing as a full doctor when necessary, though patients often complain about its apparent lack of compassion. The model was eventually replaced by the more advanced ",{"tag":"a","children":["FX-7 Medical Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/FX-7_Medical_Droid","referenceId":"reference:ebbfad0c4ae048c1"},", and later the ",{"tag":"a","children":["2-1B Medical Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/2-1B_Medical_Droid","referenceId":"reference:db368b8c0da70c7f"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["FX-6 Medical Droids can't be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["FX-6 Medical Droid Statistics (CL 0)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["1st-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/1st-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +1; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darkvision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darkvision"